      {
        "id": "char_1",
        "type": "characterization",
        "method_name": "Raman",
        "is_reported": true,
        "characterization_summary": "Temperature-dependent Raman spectra (RT to 800°C) show monoclinic-to-orthorhombic transition ~300°C (low frequency modes 34/60 cm⁻¹ → ~40 cm⁻¹) and orthorhombic-to-tetragonal transition at 740°C (710 cm⁻¹ mode disappears, low Raman activity in tetragonal phase).",
        "evidence_snippet": "The Evolution of Raman spectra for pure W O_3 in the temperature range from 13 to 475 °C is shown in Fig. 1. ... both stretching modes at 700 and 800 cm⁻¹ are no more detectable at 800 °C: the lower frequency mode at 700 cm⁻¹ disappears already at temperatures below the transition point 740 °C.",
        "related_images": [
          "22643c9328a78c33cc9dc2240dceb37c9fd20a3e20cab6e390b0ef5952d9b64e.jpg",
          "8edde5302855f2a553fa817df03eb9cc3821afc0de79715d977730eb4ec7268b.jpg"
        ],
