      {
        "id": "char_2",
        "type": "characterization",
        "method_name": "Raman",
        "is_reported": true,
        "characterization_summary": "Room temperature Raman spectra of H_xWO3 (x≤0.23) during de-hydrogenation show 710 cm⁻¹ mode decrease/disappearance and highest stretching mode shift from 816 cm⁻¹ (tetragonal x=0.23) to 806 cm⁻¹ (monoclinic WO3), with better resolution than high-T pure WO3.",
        "evidence_snippet": "The Raman spectra (see Fig. 4) show an evolution quite similar... the 710 cm⁻¹ mode decreases strongly with respect to the 816 cm⁻¹ mode upon hydrogen insertion, and disappears... its frequency decreases from 816 cm⁻¹ in H_0.23 W O_3 to 806 cm⁻¹ in monoclinic (I) W O_3."
      },
      {
        "id": "char_3",
        "type": "characterization",
        "method_name": "XRD",
        "is_reported": true,
        "characterization_summary": "Powder XRD patterns confirm phase evolution: tetragonal H_xWO3 x≈0.23 (JCPDF-ICDD 20-483), orthorhombic H_xWO3 x≈0.1 (JCPDF-ICDD 6-210), monoclinic(I) pure WO3; recorded at RT, 2θ=20-65°, Cu Kα, Δ2θ=0.05°.",
        "evidence_snippet": "Pure and hydrogenated tungsten oxide samples were analyzed by powder X-ray diffraction (XRD)... The X-ray diffractograms were recorded at RT in the angle range 2θ=20-65° and a step Δ(2θ)=0.05°. ... Fig. 3.",
